Inspiration: In Pluribus, there are really subtle one-line hints at future twists or reveals — for example, "the antenna must be as large as Africa" or "all the cell towers are down right now." Aim for this same style of understated foreshadowing. (human)

Inspiration: Project Hail Mary keeps the tone light even while dealing with epic, high-stakes subject matter. The movie delivers a series of big reveals, but doesn't linger too long on any single one — they land and keep moving. Despite this brisk reveal pacing, it's still a 2.5-hour film. (human)

